The `jev_ultrafast` package is the browser agent this project was built around:
the actor loop, the CDP adapter, the model transport and the prompts. It was
imported from browser-use/jev-ultrafast at commit
452c1ad2dd628008f1d5608f28158d76e49e6cc0 and is kept under its own name rather
than absorbed, so that its provenance stays visible in the source tree.

It has since been modified in this fork. The changes are limited and are
recorded in the Git history; the most substantial is that `jev_ultrafast/model.py`
now carries a provider's 4xx response body into the raised error, because that
body is often the only available diagnosis of a rejected request.

The `journey_evals` package -- the journey and agent evaluation runtime, the
reporting and evidence model, the budgeting, the consoles and the command line
interface -- is this project's own work.

Both are distributed under the MIT License. See LICENSE.

